## Phase 11: CSS Parser Enhancements
### Spec References
- CSS Syntax Level 3: https://www.w3.org/TR/css-syntax-3/

### 11.7.5 Error Recovery and Parse Errors ✓
- [x] Handle unmatched <}-token>, <)-token>, <]-token> via parser error reporting
- [x] CheckUnmatchedClosingBracket() and CheckBadToken() static helpers
- [x] Updated Consume_Rule_List, Consume_Style_Block_Contents, Consume_Decleration_List
- [x] Error reporter propagation through all Consume_* methods
- [x] Tests for unmatched closing bracket error reporting (12 new tests)

### 11.7.6 Convert Exceptions to Error Reporting ✓
Convert remaining CssSyntaxErrorException throws to use ICssParseErrorReporter with graceful recovery.
- [x] Parse_Rule(): UNEXPECTED_EOF, CANT_CONSUME_QUALIFIED_RULE, EOF_EXPECTED → returns null + reports error
- [x] Parse_Decleration(): EXPECTING_IDENT, CANT_CONSUME_DECLERATION → returns null + reports error
- [x] Parse_ComponentValue(): UNEXPECTED_EOF, CANT_CONSUME_COMPONENT_VALUE, EOF_EXPECTED → returns null + reports error
- [x] Consume_CssValue(): Bad_Url token, invalid hex color, unhandled token → returns CssValue.Null + reports error
- [x] Media parsing: EXPECTING_IDENT, invalid combinators, missing parens → returns MediaQuery.NotAll or breaks gracefully
- [x] Consume_Media_Feature(): EXPECTING_COMPARATOR, UNEXPECTED_TOKEN → returns null or CssValue.Null
- [x] Added ECssParseErrorType values: UnexpectedEof, ExtraContentAfterRule, ExpectedIdentifier, InvalidDeclaration, InvalidComponentValue, InvalidMediaQuery, InvalidMediaFeature, ExpectedComparator, UnexpectedToken
- [x] Added CssParseError factory methods for all new error types
- [x] Added MediaQuery.NotAll static property for invalid queries
- [x] Tests for graceful error recovery (10 new tests in CssParseErrorRecoveryTests)

### 11.7.7 Production Matching Integration
- [ ] Integrate with CSS Nesting (Phase 11.9)
  - [ ] Use ECssBlockContentsType for nested rule parsing
  - [ ] Distinguish style-block vs rule-list contexts

