### 14.5 Multi-Pass Layout Pipeline Architecture
Refactor Run_Event_Loop from single TreeWalker pass into three distinct passes.
This fixes the infinite loop caused by flag propagation during TreeWalker iteration.
Spec Reference: https://www.w3.org/TR/CSS2/visudet.html (width/height calculation order)

#### 14.5.1 Collect-Then-Process Infrastructure ✓
- [x] Create CollectDirtyNodes() helper that snapshots nodes with given flags into List<Node>
- [x] Use tree-order traversal for top-down passes (parents before children)
- [x] Create depth-sorted list helper for bottom-up passes (deepest first)
- [x] Remove FilterNodeUpdate usage from event loop (no longer needed with snapshots)

#### 14.5.2 Pass 1: Box Generation (Top-Down) ✓
- [x] Create Pass_BoxGeneration() method in Document.cs
- [x] Collect nodes with NeedsBoxUpdate | ChildNeedsBoxUpdate flags
- [x] Process in tree order (parents before children)
- [x] Call CssBoxTree.Generate_Tree() for each dirty node
- [x] Clear NeedsBoxUpdate and ChildNeedsBoxUpdate after processing each node

#### 14.5.3 Pass 2: Style Cascade (Top-Down) ✓
- [x] Create Pass_StyleCascade() method in Document.cs
- [x] Collect nodes with NeedsStyleUpdate | ChildNeedsStyleUpdate | DirectChildNeedsStyleUpdate flags
- [x] Process in tree order (parents before children)
- [ ] Call Style.Cascade() for each dirty element to recompute CSS computed values
- [x] Clear NeedsStyleUpdate, ChildNeedsStyleUpdate, DirectChildNeedsStyleUpdate after processing

#### 14.5.4 Pass 3: Layout/Reflow (Width Top-Down, Height Bottom-Up) ✓
- [x] Create Pass_Layout() method in Document.cs
- [x] Collect nodes with NeedsReflow | ChildNeedsReflow flags
- [x] Sub-pass 3a (Width Resolution - Top-Down):
  - [x] Process in tree order (parents before children)
  - [x] Call BoxModel.ResolveWidth() for each element with box
  - [ ] Wire IntrinsicSizeCalculator.Calculate() for width: auto (shrink-to-fit)
- [x] Sub-pass 3b (Height Resolution + Flow - Bottom-Up):
  - [x] Process depth-sorted (deepest nodes first)
  - [x] Call FormattingContext.Flow() to position children, get content size
  - [x] Call BoxModel.ResolveHeight() using content height for height: auto
- [x] Clear NeedsReflow and ChildNeedsReflow after processing

#### 14.5.5 BoxModel.Resolve() Refactoring ✓
- [x] Extract BoxModel.ResolveWidth() from existing Resolve() method
  - [x] Resolve horizontal dimensions: width, margin-left, margin-right, left, right
  - [x] Handle all display types (inline, block, inline-block, absolute, etc.)
  - [x] Integrate IntrinsicSizeCalculator for shrink-to-fit width
- [x] Extract BoxModel.ResolveHeight() from existing Resolve() method
  - [x] Resolve vertical dimensions: height, margin-top, margin-bottom, top, bottom
  - [x] Accept contentHeight parameter for height: auto resolution
- [x] Keep existing Resolve() as convenience method calling both

#### 14.5.6 FormattingContext.Flow() Return Type ✓
- [x] Change IFormattingContext.Flow() return type from void to Rect2f
- [x] Update FlexFormattingContext.Flow() to return content dimensions
- [x] Update GridFormattingContext.Flow() to return content dimensions
- [x] Update BlockFormattingContext.Flow() to return content dimensions
- [x] Use returned height for resolving container's height: auto

#### 14.5.7 Run_Event_Loop() Orchestration ✓
- [x] Refactor Run_Event_Loop() to call passes in sequence:
  - [x] Pass_BoxGeneration() - generates box tree from DOM
  - [x] Pass_StyleCascade() - recomputes CSS computed values
  - [x] Pass_Layout() - resolves used values and positions boxes
- [x] Remove safety iteration limit (no longer needed with snapshot approach)
- [x] Remove single TreeWalker loop

#### 14.5.8 Layout Cycle Detection
